    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d834">

                <pb facs="0684" n="676" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg676"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/2063: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-21T16:00:00+08:00">September 21, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 21—12:29 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>698. Bennett<anchor n="15" xml:id="d834-f1"/> informs me informally that pressure
                    is being applied on Chinese members of the China Foundation<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d834-f2"/> to invest $5,000,000 in Chinese Government Liberty Loan
                    bonds from the endowment funds of both indemnity remissions. [J. A.] Mackay and
                    [S. T. Bitting?] as members of the Finance Committee insist that Foundation must
                    first approve and in anticipation of the application wish to learn unofficially
                    whether the American Government believes it has the right and wishes to object
                    to investments of this sort. My own feeling is that our Government having either
                    explicitly or tacitly assented to the authority of the Foundation trustees in
                    such matters should express no opinion but I respectfully request that the
                    Department indicate what reply I should make to this question.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d834-f1" n="15" xml:id="d834-f1-content">
                <p>C. R. Bennett, representative in China of the American Group, China
                    Consortium.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d834-f2" n="16" xml:id="d834-f2-content">
                <p>China Foundation for the Promotion of Education and Culture, of which Mr. Bennett
                    was a trustee.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
